['pairs',['换成官方示例 [2,1,3]，二进制是 10、01、11。掩码是表示哪些位为 1 的整数。令 f[m] 为按位与恰好等于掩码 m 的有序数对 (i,j) 的个数。按行 i、按列 j，九个结果是 [2,0,2]、[0,1,1]、[2,1,3]，所以 f=[2,3,3,1]。例如 m=0 有 (0,1)、(1,0) 两对，必须保留次数。','Use the official [2,1,3] example, binary 10, 01, 11. A mask is an integer specifying which bits are 1. Let f[m] count ordered pairs (i,j) with AND exactly m. With rows i and columns j, the nine results are [2,0,2], [0,1,1], [2,1,3], giving f=[2,3,3,1]. Mask 0 has two pairs, (0,1) and (1,0); their multiplicity must survive.']],
['pairScan',['固定第三个值 x=2（10）：m 只能是 0（00）或 1（01），贡献 f[0]+f[1]=2+3=5。x=1 贡献 f[0]+f[2]=5；x=3 仅贡献 f[0]=2，总计 12。先用 O(n²) 建表，再为每个 x 扫所有 U 个掩码，是 O(n²+nU) 时间、O(U) 空间；U 是可能掩码的数量。下一步把反复求和也合并。','Fix third value x=2 (10): only m=0 (00) or m=1 (01) works, contributing f[0]+f[1]=2+3=5. For x=1 the contribution is f[0]+f[2]=5; for x=3 it is f[0]=2, totaling 12. Build f in O(n²), then scan all U masks for each x: O(n²+nU) time and O(U) space, where U is the number of possible masks. Next we combine the repeated sums too.']],
['wrong',['错误捷径：只保留 AND 已经为 0 的数对？[3,5,6] 中 3&5=1，3&6=2，5&6=4，所有数对 AND 都非零，但 3&5&6=0。第三个数仍可能清掉剩余的位。另一个错误是用集合去重；[0,0,0] 有 27 个位置三元组，而不是一个。','Tempting shortcut: keep only pairs whose AND is already zero? In [3,5,6], 3&5=1, 3&6=2, and 5&6=4. No pair AND is zero, yet 3&5&6=0. The third value can still clear the remaining bits. Deduplicating values is also wrong: [0,0,0] has 27 index triples, not one.']],
['s2',['03 · 怎样一次求出所有兼容数对总数？','03 · How can we precompute every compatible-pair total?']],
['derive',['这一节用 f[m] 表示按位与恰为 m 的有序数对次数，g 是将要构造的求和表。固定第三个值 x 时，数对掩码 m 的 1 只能放在 x 的 0 位上。令 B 为最大值的二进制位数，至少为 1；U=2ᴮ，full=U−1 是 B 个 1。有限位补集 s=full^x 把这 B 位内的 0、1 互换（^ 是异或）。例如 x=2（10），s=1（01）。m 是 s 的子掩码，意思是 m 只使用 s 允许的 1 位。','Here f[m] counts ordered pairs whose AND is exactly m, and g is the sum table we will build. For a fixed third value x, a pair mask m may have 1-bits only where x has 0-bits. Let B be the bit length of the maximum value, at least 1; U=2ᴮ and full=U−1 has B ones. The finite complement s=full^x flips those B bits (^ is XOR). For x=2 (10), s=1 (01). A submask m of s uses only the 1-bits allowed by s.']],
